        "In the 1700s, Great Britain ruled thirteen colonies along the eastern coast of North America. Over time, many colonists grew angry that they were taxed by a distant government in which they had no representatives.",
        "The slogan 'no taxation without representation' captured their frustration. Protests, such as the Boston Tea Party, showed growing resistance. In 1775, fighting broke out between colonial militias and British troops.",
        "In 1776, the colonies adopted the Declaration of Independence, written mainly by Thomas Jefferson. It announced that the colonies were free and independent states and stated that people have rights that governments must protect.",
        "The war that followed was long and difficult. With leadership from George Washington and help from allies such as France, the Americans eventually defeated the British.",
